text @[Yoshino]
text We should cover the area with a sheet.
text Yoshino-san gets me to hold the tools and explains everything step by step as he works.
text The two of us remove the heavy indoor unit together, then insert a new brace.
text But then, there seems to be a problem with how strong the ceiling is, and Yoshino-san starts to undo it.
sound MMQ.aac
text @[Yoshino]
text Take a look, Okazaki.
text I climb up and peer behind the dark opening leading to the area behind the ceiling.
text It's like a different world. I've never seen anything like it before.
text Thin, long metallic braces are supporting the ceiling, and cords have been strung across beams that follow them.
text Dust that has gathered over many years reflects in the beam of my flashlight and sparkles.
sound MMR.aac
text @[Yoshino]
text Ceilings are more fragile than you'd think.
sound MMS.aac
text @[Yoshino]
text They're just hung up on the braces, so cables always go with the beams or pillars, right?
sound MMT.aac
text @[Yoshino]
text Air conditioners are the same way. You just have to spread the weight out across braces when you hang them and you'll be fine.
sound MMU.aac
text @[Yoshino]
text You just need to watch for now. Even watching once will definitely help you out.
text @[Tomoya]
text Ah, got it.
text Then, Yoshino-san returns to his work.
