text I've hung the futon. I've washed our clothes.
text With nothing left to do, I sit there blankly staring at the TV.
text @[Tomoya]
text (What am I doing? Nagisa is busy working away at her mock exams right now...)
text @[Tomoya]
text (Well, I work hard on the weekdays, so I guess just hanging out is fine...)
text After the news break ends, a cooking show begins.
text The screen shows today's menu: a simple bowl of fried rice.
text @[Tomoya]
text I could probably make something that basic with what we have lying around.
text By the time I notice, it's noon and I've memorized how to make the dish.
text Time to put what I've learned to the test.
text While cooking was never my strong suit, making the fried rice is so easy I feel let down.
text They didn't call it simple for nothing.
text I try tasting it, and it's not bad.
text @[Tomoya]
text (I could easily eat this the next few times I'm alone, at least.)
text Just as I go to put it on my plate...
